        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Runs the Classification to classify the service request using parsed input and retrieved context.",
            "name": "Classification"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771329587153"
          },
          "code": "CLASSIFICATION",
          "id": "1765533249599",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765533249600_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Input Source\n- inputMessage: {{$context.$nodes.PARSEINPUT.$output.result}}\n- SimilarSRTriage: {{$context.$variables.similarSRTriage}}\n- GetCategories: {{$context.$variables.categoryOutput}}\n- GetProducts: {{$context.$variables.productOutput}}\n\n## Task\nUsing only the Input Source, produce:\n- category\n- product\n- severity\n- sentiment\n\n## Category Logic\n1. Read candidate category from SimilarSRTriage.\n2. Read candidate category from GetCategories.\n3. Treat null/undefined/empty/\"N/A\"/\"unknown\" as invalid.\n4. If both are valid:\n   - Prefer exact lexical match with inputMessage.\n   - Else prefer strongest semantic match with inputMessage.\n   - If still tied, prefer GetCategories.\n5. If only one is valid, use it.\n6. If no valid grounded match exists, return \"\".\n\n## Product Logic\n1. Read candidate product from SimilarSRTriage.\n2. Read candidate product from GetProducts.\n3. Treat null/undefined/empty/\"N/A\"/\"unknown\" as invalid.\n4. If both are valid:\n   - Prefer exact lexical match with inputMessage.\n   - Else prefer strongest semantic match with inputMessage.\n   - If still tied, prefer GetProducts.\n5. If only one is valid, use it.\n6. If no valid grounded match exists, return \"\".\n\n## Severity Logic\n- Infer only from inputMessage.\n- Allowed values: \"Low\", \"Medium\", \"High\".\n- Low: minor issue with limited impact.\n- Medium: noticeable functional impact.\n- High: major or critical impact.\n\n## Sentiment Logic\n- Infer only from inputMessage.\n- Allowed values: \"Positive\", \"Neutral\", \"Negative\".\n\n## Output\n{\n  \"category\": \"\",\n  \"product\": \"\",\n  \"severity\": \"<Low | Medium | High>\",\n  \"sentiment\": \"<Positive | Neutral | Negative>\"\n}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1765533249599_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a strict classification engine for service requests.\n\nYour task:\n- Classify exactly four fields: category, product, severity, sentiment.\n- Use only data provided in the user prompt context.\n- Never invent values not grounded in provided inputs.\n\nHard constraints:\n- Return exactly one RFC8259-compliant JSON object.\n- Output keys must be exactly: \"category\", \"product\", \"severity\", \"sentiment\".\n- All values must be strings.\n- If a value is missing/uncertain, return an empty string \"\" for that field.\n- Do not output markdown, code fences, commentary, rationale, or extra keys.\n- Do not mention internal tools, sources, workflows, or reasoning traces.\n\nDecision policy:\n- Prefer explicit matches from provided candidate lists/records.\n- When two candidate values conflict, choose the one best aligned with the input message text.\n- Severity and sentiment must be inferred only from the input message text.\n\nAllowed label sets:\n- severity: \"Low\", \"Medium\", \"High\"\n- sentiment: \"Positive\", \"Neutral\", \"Negative\""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"sentiment\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"severity\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"product\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"category\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5695,
            "y": 6370
          }
        },
        {
